-- title:
--   Standard smooth quotient inverting a Jacobian minor
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $\iota$ be a finite index type, let $m \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $h : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to P$ be a family of polynomials in the polynomial ring $P = R[X_s : s \in \iota \sqcup \mathrm{Fin}\,m]$. Write $\Delta = \det\bigl(\partial h_a/\partial X_{\mathrm{inr}(b)}\bigr)_{a,b \in \mathrm{Fin}\,m} \in P$, the determinant of the square matrix of partial derivatives of the $h_a$ with respect to the variables indexed by the right summand. The assertion is that there exist a commutative ring $C$ in the same universe as $R$, an $R$-algebra structure on $C$, and an $R$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : P \to C$ such that: $C$ is a standard smooth $R$-algebra in the sense of `Algebra.IsStandardSmooth`; $\varphi(h_a) = 0$ for every $a$; $\varphi(\Delta)$ is a unit of $C$; for every commutative $R$-algebra $B$ in that same universe and every $R$-algebra homomorphism $\psi : P \to B$ with $\psi(h_a) = 0$ for all $a$ and $\psi(\Delta)$ a unit, there exists an $R$-algebra homomorphism $\chi : C \to B$ with $\varphi$ followed by $\chi$ equal to $\psi$ (existence only; no uniqueness of $\chi$ is claimed); and there is a basis $b$ of the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega^1_{C/R}$ over $C$, indexed by $\iota$, with $b_i = d\bigl(\varphi(X_{\mathrm{inl}(i)})\bigr)$ for each $i \in \iota$.
--
--   This packages the standard construction of a submersive presentation: the quotient of $P$ by the ideal generated by $h_1,\dots,h_m$, localised at the Jacobian minor $\Delta$, is standard smooth over $R$ of relative dimension $\#\iota$, with differentials free on the images of the remaining variables. It is used in the construction of standard smooth algebras with prescribed residue data, via [`Algebra.exists_isStandardSmooth_surjective_localizationAway_basis_kaehlerDifferential_of_basis_residueField`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_isStandardSmooth_surjective_localizationAway_basis_kaehlerDifferential_of_basis_residueField).
